{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793899861203800002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"nickelic-lazuline-gonolek","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"32ffc939ca44a6fc2bb397842c55bef952731db1100591711b7b2f5fe325a668","event_uuid":"48eb8df1-4698-4773-b665-2173291cd640","position":{"commit_sha":"5beaa5662f2529c6766a6f862c5216293628f085","position":"1793899841880676001-48eb8df1-4698-4773-b665-2173291cd640"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"8ed47e085790e6e919e7d3ca4cb1dcc172b7c846153e8f167abcffcda21dd674","event_uuid":"e3013304-4d02-40db-94e4-a28d88fc19b2","position":{"commit_sha":"10e36d4bb56adc6bad5e64399196c5816ceb16ca","position":"1793899861203800001-e3013304-4d02-40db-94e4-a28d88fc19b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793899841880676001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e3013304-4d02-40db-94e4-a28d88fc19b2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"467d-e068-ee33-4bad"}],"description":"## Observation (read-only, production MCP host i-00880b2c7f13527c5, 2026-11-05)\n\nThe production MCP tickets clone (`/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`, container label `rebar.service=mcp`) has received no git object maintenance since early September:\n\n- `git count-objects -v`: 74,605 loose objects (8.63 GiB loose), 235 packs (2.16 GiB), 306,528 commits.\n- `.git/objects/info/commit-graph` dated 2026-08-31; `objects/info/packs` dated 2026-09-02.\n- Local operator checkout of the same history: 6 packs, 333 MiB loose, current commit-graph chain.\n\nHistory walks there are much slower than on a clone of the same history:\n\n| walk (same command as rebar.attest.authorship_resolution) | production (shared clone in the container) | operator clone |\n|---|---|---|\n| store-wide `build_position_commit_map` (`-- '*.json'`) | 427.5 s | 111 s (bug breezelike-travelsick-moray, 2026-11-03 comment) |\n| per-ticket map, 26a0-0104-9b63-4500 | 160.8 s | 19.1 s |\n| per-ticket map, fb16-a8b0-c2b7-449a | 266.1 s | not measured |\n\nThe store-wide walk exceeds its 300 s timeout in production, so the compaction sweep's shared position map is always `None` there and every fold falls back to a per-ticket walk. Bug breezelike-travelsick-moray moves that walk outside the store write lock; it does not make the walk faster, so a production sweep still spends minutes per ticket before each fold.\n\nStore commits run with automatic maintenance disabled (`_AUTOMAINT_OFF` in compact.py and the commit seam), and `gc.autodetach=false`, `maintenance.autodetach=false` are set on the clone. Unverified: which component, if any, is meant to repack or rewrite the commit-graph on the production clone, and whether the 2 vCPU host or the 3.6 GiB container memory cap also contribute.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe production tickets clone's object store stays packed with a current commit-graph, so path-limited history walks cost about what they cost on a fresh clone, and the store-wide position walk finishes inside its timeout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The mechanism that should keep the production tickets clone packed (or its absence) is identified with evidence.\n- [ ] After the fix, production `git count-objects -v` shows loose objects bounded and the commit-graph current, measured read-only via SSM.\n- [ ] The store-wide position walk completes inside its 300 s timeout in production, measured on a shared clone in the container.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"51e0-5038-bf00-4653","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Production MCP tickets clone gets no git maintenance; history walks 4-8x slower and the sweep position map times out","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["48eb8df1-4698-4773-b665-2173291cd640","e3013304-4d02-40db-94e4-a28d88fc19b2"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793899861203800002,"uuid":"5185e585-2596-493e-ab75-281adf8393db"}